BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ics Kstx8Swyw669Kakgqa 6478083 Ics": "https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2131910341"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ics_kstx8swyw669kakgqa_6478083_ics
SUMMARY:Selichot - Service\, Dinner\, Music!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T213000
DTSTAMP:20260730T032210Z
UID:TU2131910341
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T183000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260714T210247Z
DESCRIPTION:Welcome in the spirit of the High Holidays with a participator
 y\, music-filled night! Connect with the Shomrei community over dinner\, s
 ing High Holiday melodies\, and have some fun at our jazz dessert receptio
 n.\n\n**RSVP Required for Dinner and Reception** http://shomrei.org/jazz\n
 \nFree or Suggested Donation:  \n$20 per adult\, $10 per child over 12\, $
 36 per family\n\n**------------------------------  \nAdults and Kids 8+ (Y
 ounger Kids/Scroll Down)**  \n6:30 Welcome   \n6:45 Dinner (Middle Eastern
  dairy dinner)  \n8:00 Havdalah and Selichot Service  \n9:00 Dessert and J
 azz Reception\n\nAs Shabbat comes to a close\, children and adults will co
 me together to recite Havdalah prayers. We are looking forward to having o
 ur children who are 8 yrs old and up help lead the havdalah candle lightin
 g ceremony while reciting prayers with Rabbi Julie.\n\nParticipatory\, mus
 ic-filled service led by Rabbi Julie\, Talia Lakritz\, Suzanna Grobman\, D
 ebra Caplan and accompanied by Oren Neiman and his jazz ensemble.\n\nThe p
 arty continues with a dessert reception. Live music will be provided by th
 e jazz ensemble.\n\nStreaming: http://shomrei.org/live\n\n**--------------
 ----------------**\n\n**Kids 7 and Younger**  \n6:30 Little Kid's Dinner  
  \n7:00 Free Play  \n7:30 Selichot Inspired Art Activity  \n8:00 Children 
 welcome to stay in childcare\, or join Selichot service\n\n**-------------
 -----------------**\n\n**Have questions? Want to Help out? Contact:** Shom
 rei Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(973) 746-5031\n\n**What is Selichot?*
 *  \nThe Hebrew word selichah means “forgiveness.” The plural form of 
 the word selichah is selichot\, a word traditionally used to refer to addi
 tional prayers for forgiveness recited during the month of Elul (through Y
 om Kippur). We gather together on the Saturday night before Rosh Hashanah 
 to meditate on the capacity for forgiveness and on its power. In joining t
 ogether we help each other pray for that blessing – to give it and to re
 ceive it.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260728T173440Z
LOCATION:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2131910341
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
X-TEAMUP-ROOM:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah
END:VEVENT
