X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10340
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10340
DTSTART:20261119T150000Z
DTEND:20261119T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261119T000000Z
SUMMARY:Morning Book Club
DESCRIPTION:November 19 Hotel on the Corner of Bitter & Sweet by Jamie 
 Ford\n\nIn 1986\, Henry Lee joins a crowd outside the Panama Hotel\, once 
 the gateway to Seattle's Japantown. The new owner has discovered the 
 belongings of Japanese families who were sent to internment camps. Henry\, 
 a Chinese American\, remembers a young Japanese American girl from his 
 childhood in the 1940s—Keiko Okabe\, with whom he forged a bond of 
 friendship and innocent love. After Keiko and her family were evacuated to 
 the internment camps\, she and Henry could only hope that their promise to 
 each other would be kept. Now\, forty years later\, Henry explores the 
 hotel's basement for the Okabe family's belongings and for a long-lost 
 object whose value he cannot even begin to measure. His search will take 
 him on a journey to revisit the sacrifices he has made for family\, love\, 
 country.
LOCATION:West Caldwell - New Book Area
ORGANIZER;CN="West Caldwell Public Library":MAILTO:programs@westcaldwell.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10340-17032141
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17032141
END:VEVENT
